			</ADDITIONAL-PROPERTIES>
			<DESCRIPTION>
				<PLAIN-TEXT>&quot;The System Capability Mapping Viewpoint describes the relationships of System Capabilities. The reasoning for System Capabilities as support for System Use Cases and the contribution of System Processes to Capabilities are described. Furthermore, the mapping of System Capabilities to Operational Capabilities are identified.Representation:A tabular format listing the relationships of System Capabilities to Operational Capabilities, System Use Cases, System Process Activities, and System Requirements.&quot;</PLAIN-TEXT>
			</DESCRIPTION>
		</ELEMENT>
		<ELEMENT>
			<ID>2316658_pDnuAbU4Ee6Ru6Ifm1D6NA</ID>
			<RHP-ID>GUID f8ee7d93-89b6-4ab8-9ee8-fe506f771c94</RHP-ID>
			<NAME>SAF_L2_LSTD</NAME>
			<TYPE>Stereotype</TYPE>
			<TYPE-ID>GUID_8e474b0d-df37-464a-90d9-88a054f5ec8a_1615988136</TYPE-ID>
			<DISPLAY-TYPE>Stereotype</DISPLAY-TYPE>
			<DISPLAY-GROUP>Stereotypes</DISPLAY-GROUP>
			<BROWSER-ICON>Stereotype~ALL~BrowserIcon</BROWSER-ICON>
			<GROUP-ICON>Stereotype~ALL~GroupIcon</GROUP-ICON>
			<IS-TOP-LEVEL>false</IS-TOP-LEVEL>
			<MODIFIED-TIME-UTC>2026/10/19 6:31:38</MODIFIED-TIME-UTC>
			<VIEW-PARENTS></VIEW-PARENTS>
			<VIEW-CHILDREN></VIEW-CHILDREN>
			<AGGREGATES>I:2316696_pDnuAbU4Ee6Ru6Ifm1D6NA</AGGREGATES>
			<REFERENCES>
				<BASE-STEREOTYPES>
					<VALUE-IDS>GUID_6c142614-3349-49e9-8c6b-0236be5f6b61_1612371150</VALUE-IDS>
				</BASE-STEREOTYPES>
			</REFERENCES>
			<ADDITIONAL-PROPERTIES>
				<TYPE-GROUP-LABEL>SAF_L2_LSTD - Logical Structure Definition</TYPE-GROUP-LABEL>
			</ADDITIONAL-PROPERTIES>
			<DESCRIPTION>
				<PLAIN-TEXT>&quot;The Logical Structure Definition Viewpoint describes how the system is decomposed into a hierarchical structure of logical elements responsible for different system functions (divide &amp; conquer principle). It covers related logical concepts and principles that support the logical operation of the system and is widely reusable among similar systems like product families, or product generations.Representation:A block definition diagram (BDD) featuring the logical system block and logical blocks for any kind of logical element the system is composed of. These elements are connected to the system block by means of aggregation relationships. Note: Multiple relationships to a kind of element are allowed meaning, that this kind of element is used in several roles.&quot;</PLAIN-TEXT>
			</DESCRIPTION>
		</ELEMENT>
